// A type used by more than one file lives in its domain's `types/`
// folder, one type per file, named after it. `weigh_flour` and
// `price_flour` both use `SackWeight`, so it lives here rather than in
// either of them.
//
// A weight is a quantity, so it is built on the standard `Mass` rather than
// on a bare number: the unit is part of every value (`500g`, `2kg`), and a
// weight can never be mixed up with a temperature or a count.

/// The weight of a delivery of flour. Never negative, with no upper limit.
type SackWeight = Mass {
    min: 0g
}
